{"command": "cd "$WORKSPACE_DIR/build" && cat > lease_06.txt <<'EOF'
@H1 ARTICLE 15 — TITLE; PERMITTED EXCEPTIONS; REPRESENTATIONS
@H2 15.1 Title
@P Landlord represents, warrants, and covenants that, as of the Commencement Date and throughout the Term: (a) Landlord holds fee simple title to the Premises free and clear of all liens, encumbrances, and exceptions other than the Permitted Exceptions; (b) Landlord has full right, power, and authority to enter into and perform this Lease; (c) no other lease, license, or occupancy agreement affecting the Premises is in effect; (d) there is no pending or, to Landlord's knowledge, threatened litigation, condemnation (other than the 2012 acquisition), or governmental proceeding affecting the Premises that would materially and adversely affect Tenant's leasehold interest; (e) Landlord's acquisition of the Premises by condemnation did not create, and no instrument of record creates, any reversionary interest, right of reverter, or condition subsequent in favor of any former owner or other Person that would be triggered by the lease of the Premises to Tenant or by the development of the Project; and (f) Landlord has not received notice of any violation of Applicable Law affecting the Premises that has not been cured.
@H2 15.2 Permitted Exceptions
@P Tenant accepts the Premises subject only to the Permitted Exceptions listed on **Exhibit B**. Landlord shall, at its sole cost, cause the following to be removed, discharged, or bonded off as a condition precedent to the Commencement Date: (a) the Mechanics' Lien described in Section 15.4; and (b) any other lien, encumbrance, or exception that is not a Permitted Exception. Tenant shall have the right to object, in its reasonable discretion, to any exception disclosed by any updated commitment or survey, and Landlord shall, at its election, cure such exception or cause the Title Company to insure over it.
@NOTE The Term Sheet (Section 13) lists the $187,500 mechanics' lien filed by Calloway Marine Demolition Inc. as a "Permitted Exception." It should not be. The Title Company will not issue a policy while the lien is of record (Schedule B-I, Requirement No. 7), and the lien arises from work performed for the fee owner before this transaction. See Drafting Issues Memo, Item 18.
@H2 15.3 Title Insurance
@P Landlord shall cooperate with Tenant, at Tenant's cost, in obtaining an ALTA Leasehold Owner's Policy in the amount of $425,000,000 (and such additional amounts as Tenant may reasonably request) from Ridgepoint Title & Escrow Co., together with the ALTA 13-06 (Leasehold — Owner's), ALTA 9-06 (Restrictions, Encroachments, Minerals), ALTA 17-06 (Access and Entry), ALTA 25-06 (Same as Survey), and Zoning endorsements, subject only to the Permitted Exceptions. Landlord shall execute such affidavits, indemnities, and instruments as the Title Company may reasonably require, including an owner's affidavit, a non-foreign status certification, and a gap indemnity.
@H2 15.4 Mechanics' Lien
@P Landlord shall, on or before the Commencement Date, cause the Mechanics' Lien filed by Calloway Marine Demolition Inc. on April 3, 2025 in the amount of $187,500, recorded at Volume 418, Page 302 of the Port Calloway Land Records, to be discharged of record or bonded off in accordance with Conn. Gen. Stat. § 49-37. If Landlord fails to do so, Tenant may (a) postpone the Commencement Date without liability, (b) discharge or bond off the lien and offset the cost (including any bond premium and reasonable attorneys' fees) against Base Rent, and (c) pursue any other remedy available under this Lease or Applicable Law. Landlord shall indemnify Tenant against all loss arising from such lien.
@H2 15.5 Quiet Enjoyment
@P Landlord covenants that, so long as no Event of Default by Tenant exists, Tenant shall peaceably and quietly have, hold, and enjoy the Premises and the Improvements during the Term without hindrance or interruption by Landlord or any Person claiming by, through, or under Landlord, subject to the Permitted Exceptions and Applicable Law.
@H2 15.6 Landlord's Representations and Warranties
@P Landlord represents and warrants to Tenant that, as of the Effective Date and the Commencement Date:
@C1 (a) Landlord is a public body corporate and politic duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under Conn. Gen. Stat. § 8-125 *et seq.*, and has all requisite power and authority to own the Premises and to enter into, execute, deliver, and perform this Lease;
@C1 (b) the execution, delivery, and performance of this Lease have been duly authorized by all necessary action of Landlord, including the adoption of Resolution No. 2025-047 by Landlord's Board of Commissioners, and no further approval, authorization, public hearing, referendum, or consent is required for Landlord to perform its obligations under this Lease;
@C1 (c) this Lease constitutes the legal, valid, and binding obligation of Landlord, enforceable against Landlord in accordance with its terms, subject to bankruptcy, insolvency, and similar laws affecting creditors' rights generally and to general principles of equity;
@C1 (d) the execution, delivery, and performance of this Lease do not conflict with, or constitute a default under, Landlord's enabling legislation, bylaws, any resolution of its Board of Commissioners, any judgment or order binding on Landlord, or any instrument to which Landlord is a party;
@C1 (e) Landlord has delivered to Tenant true, correct, and complete copies of the ELUR, the Declaration of Right of First Refusal recorded at Volume 405, Page 55, the Declaration of Restrictive Covenants recorded at Volume 408, Page 230, and the Final Judgment of Condemnation by which Landlord acquired the Premises, and there are no other recorded instruments affecting the Premises other than those disclosed in Title Commitment No. TC-2025-07821;
@C1 (f) Landlord has not received any notice of any pending or threatened claim, action, or proceeding relating to the environmental condition of the Premises other than as disclosed in the Environmental Reports;
@C1 (g) the representations and warranties of Landlord in this Section 15.6 shall survive the Commencement Date and shall be deemed remade as of the Commencement Date; and
@C1 (h) Landlord has not granted, and shall not grant during the Term, any option, right of first offer, or other right to acquire the Premises (other than the Right of First Refusal) that would adversely affect Tenant's rights under this Lease.
@H2 15.7 Landlord's Fee Mortgages
@P If Landlord grants any mortgage, deed of trust, or other lien on its fee interest in the Premises (a "**Fee Mortgage**"), such Fee Mortgage shall be and remain subject and subordinate in all respects to this Lease and to the rights of Tenant and each Leasehold Mortgagee, and Landlord shall cause the holder of any Fee Mortgage to execute and deliver to Tenant and each Leasehold Mortgagee an SNDA in form reasonably satisfactory to them. Any Fee Mortgage that is not so subordinated shall be void as against Tenant's leasehold interest and the interest of each Leasehold Mortgagee to the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Law.

@H1 ARTICLE 16 — DEFAULT AND REMEDIES
@H2 16.1 Tenant Events of Default
@P Each of the following shall constitute an Event of Default by Tenant:
@C1 (a) **Monetary Default.** Tenant fails to pay any installment of Base Rent, Percentage Rent, or other Rent within ten (10) Business Days after written notice from Landlord that such amount is past due; provided that Landlord shall not be required to give more than two (2) such notices in any twelve (12) month period, after which a failure to pay within five (5) Business Days after the due date shall constitute an Event of Default without notice;
@C1 (b) **Non-Monetary Default.** Tenant fails to perform or observe any material non-monetary obligation under this Lease, and such failure continues for thirty (30) days after written notice from Landlord specifying the failure, or, if such failure cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) days, Tenant fails to commence cure within such period and thereafter diligently prosecute cure to completion;
@C1 (c) **Milestone Default.** Tenant fails to achieve Milestone 1 or Milestone 3 by the applicable Milestone Date, as extended, and such failure is not cured within the Milestone Cure Period and the Extended Cure period, and the Lender Cure Periods have expired, in each case as provided in Article 9;
@C1 (d) **Insolvency.** Tenant files a voluntary petition in bankruptcy, or an order for relief is entered against Tenant in an involuntary proceeding that is not dismissed within sixty (60) days, or Tenant makes a general assignment for the benefit of creditors, or a receiver is appointed for a substantial part of Tenant's assets and not discharged within sixty (60) days; and
@C1 (e) **Abandonment.** Tenant abandons the Premises for a continuous period of one hundred eighty (180) days, other than during a period of Force Majeure Event, Casualty, Condemnation, or restoration; provided that vacating a building for the purpose of renovation, repositioning, or re-leasing shall not constitute abandonment.
@H2 16.2 Landlord's Remedies
@P Upon the occurrence of an uncured Event of Default by Tenant, Landlord may, subject to Article 10 and Article 9:
@C1 (a) terminate this Lease by written notice, whereupon Tenant shall surrender the Premises, subject to Article 14.5 and to the rights of each Leasehold Mortgagee;
@C1 (b) recover from Tenant all Rent accrued and unpaid, together with all damages proximately caused by the Event of Default, including the reasonable costs of re-letting and the amount by which the Rent for the balance of the Term exceeds the fair rental value of the Premises for the balance of the Term, discounted to present value at a rate equal to the yield on United States Treasury obligations of comparable maturity;
@C1 (c) draw upon the Security Deposit in accordance with Article 7, limited to the amount of Landlord's actual, documented loss;
@C1 (d) pursue specific performance and injunctive relief; and
@C1 (e) pursue any other remedy available at law or in equity.
@P Landlord shall use commercially reasonable efforts to mitigate its damages. Landlord's remedies are cumulative, except that Landlord shall not recover more than once for the same loss, shall not both terminate this Lease and recover Rent for a period after termination except as damages, and shall not retain the Security Deposit as a penalty. Landlord shall not have any right to accelerate Rent, to declare the entire balance of Rent for the Term immediately due and payable, or to forfeit the Improvements.
@H2 16.3 Landlord Events of Default
@P Each of the following shall constitute an Event of Default by Landlord:
@C1 (a) Landlord fails to perform or observe any material obligation under this Lease (including the obligation to deliver an SNDA, estoppel, consent, or other instrument, to discharge the Mechanics' Lien, to perform its obligations under Article 8 or Section 8.9, or to perform any obligation relating to the Abatement Program), and such failure continues for thirty (30) days after written notice from Tenant specifying the failure, or, if such failure cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) days, Landlord fails to commence cure within such period and thereafter diligently prosecute cure to completion;
@C1 (b) Landlord breaches any representation or warranty in Section 15.1 or Section 15.6 in any material respect;
@C1 (c) Landlord wrongfully attempts to terminate this Lease, wrongfully exercises or threatens to exercise the Reverter Right, or wrongfully interferes with Tenant's quiet enjoyment of the Premises; or
@C1 (d) Landlord fails to pay any amount owing to Tenant under this Lease, including any amount owing under Section 8.4 or Section 8.7, within thirty (30) days after written demand.
@H2 16.4 Tenant's Remedies
@P Upon the occurrence of an uncured Event of Default by Landlord, Tenant may, in addition to any other remedy available at law or in equity:
@C1 (a) offset the amount of Tenant's damages against Rent next coming due, including amounts owing under Section 6.2(d), Section 7.4(d), Section 8.3, Section 8.4, Section 8.7, and Section 15.4;
@C1 (b) perform Landlord's obligation and offset the reasonable cost of such performance (together with an administrative fee equal to five percent (5%) of such cost) against Rent next coming due;
@C1 (c) seek specific performance, declaratory relief, and injunctive relief, and Landlord waives any defense based on the adequacy of a remedy at law;
@C1 (d) seek damages, including consequential damages to the extent proximately caused by Landlord's breach; and
@C1 (e) terminate this Lease, if the Event of Default is material and remains uncured for one hundred twenty (120) days after notice, in which case the Improvements shall be treated as provided in Section 14.5(b).
@P Tenant's exercise of any offset right under this Section 16.4 shall not constitute a default under this Lease, and Landlord shall, at Tenant's request, confirm in writing to each Leasehold Mortgagee that such offset is permitted under this Lease and does not constitute a default by Tenant.
