@P Tenant accepts the Premises subject only to the Permitted Exceptions listed on **Exhibit B**. Landlord shall, at its sole cost, cause the following to be removed, discharged, or bonded off as a condition precedent to the Commencement Date: (a) the Mechanics' Lien described in Section 15.4; and (b) any other lien, encumbrance, or exception that is not a Permitted Exception. Tenant shall have the right to object, in its reasonable discretion, to any exception disclosed by any updated commitment or survey, and Landlord shall, at its election, cure such exception or cause the Title Company to insure over it.
