@P The mediation requirement of Section 17.2 shall not apply to (a) any action seeking injunctive relief, specific performance, or the appointment of a receiver; (b) any exercise of a right or remedy by a Leasehold Mortgagee, or any action to foreclose or otherwise enforce a Leasehold Mortgage; (c) any action to collect Rent or to recover possession following a termination; (d) any exercise of the Reverter Right, or any challenge thereto; or (e) any determination expressly required to be made by an appraiser or accountant under this Lease.
@H2 17.4 Confidentiality
@P Each party shall keep confidential the terms of this Lease and all financial statements, rent rolls, and other information furnished by the other party, and shall not disclose the same except (a) to its officers, commissioners, employees, attorneys, accountants, consultants, lenders, investors, and prospective transferees who have a need to know, (b) as required by Applicable Law, including the Freedom of Information Act, (c) in connection with any enforcement action, financing, or sale, and (d) to the extent the information is or becomes publicly available other than through a breach of this Section.
@H2 17.5 Freedom of Information
@P Landlord acknowledges that it is a public agency subject to the Connecticut Freedom of Information Act, Conn. Gen. Stat. § 1-200 *et seq.* Landlord shall, before disclosing any information furnished by Tenant that Tenant has designated as confidential or proprietary, (a) give Tenant not less than five (5) Business Days' prior written notice (or such shorter period as may be required by law, but in no event less than twenty-four (24) hours), (b) assert in good faith all applicable exemptions, including Conn. Gen. Stat. § 1-210(b)(4) and § 1-210(b)(5), and (c) reasonably cooperate with Tenant, at Tenant's cost, in seeking a protective order, if Tenant so requests. Tenant may, at its election and cost, intervene in any FOIA proceeding to protect its information.
@H2 17.6 Estoppel Certificates
@P Each party shall, within ten (10) Business Days after request, execute and deliver an estoppel certificate certifying such matters as the requesting party (or its lender, purchaser, or Title Company) may reasonably request, including that this Lease is in full force and effect, that no default exists, and the then-current Rent. Failure to deliver within such period shall constitute an estoppel in favor of the requesting party as to the matters stated in the request unless such party delivers a written objection within such period.

@H1 ARTICLE 18 — MISCELLANEOUS
@H2 18.1 Notices
@P All notices, demands, consents, and other communications under this Lease shall be in writing and shall be deemed duly given (a) upon personal delivery, (b) one (1) Business Day after deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier, (c) three (3) Business Days after deposit in the United States mail, certified or registered, return receipt requested, postage prepaid, or (d) upon transmission by electronic mail, provided that a copy is also sent by one of the foregoing methods within two (2) Business Days, addressed as follows (or to such other address as a party may designate by notice):
@C1 **Landlord:** City of Port Calloway Redevelopment Authority, 75 Municipal Plaza, Port Calloway, Connecticut 06801, Attention: Executive Director; with a copy to Pryor Whitfield & Koss LLP, 55 Courthouse Square, Port Calloway, Connecticut 06801, Attention: Howard Koss, Esq.
@C1 **Tenant:** Meridian Gateway Holdings LLC, 400 Harborview Drive, Suite 1200, Port Calloway, Connecticut 06801, Attention: Marcus Ellison, Managing Member; with a copy to Hargrove & Linden LLP, 1100 Constitution Avenue, Hartford, Connecticut 06103, Attention: Rebecca Tsang, Esq.
@C1 **Leasehold Mortgagee:** Bayside Federal Lending Corp., 200 Atlantic Boulevard, Stamford, Connecticut 06902, Attention: Sandra Milliken, Senior Vice President, Commercial Real Estate Lending, or at such other address as the Leasehold Mortgagee may designate in writing, with a copy to the Leasehold Mortgagee's counsel.
@H2 18.2 Entire Agreement; Amendments
@P This Lease, together with its Exhibits, supersedes the Term Sheet and all prior and contemporaneous understandings and agreements, written or oral, with respect to its subject matter, and constitutes the entire agreement of the parties. This Lease may be amended only by a written instrument signed by both parties and, if any Leasehold Mortgage is in effect, consented to by each Leasehold Mortgagee in accordance with Section 10.6.
@H2 18.3 Severability; Reformation
@P If any provision of this Lease is held invalid, illegal, or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect, and the invalid or unenforceable provision shall be reformed to the minimum extent necessary to render it valid and enforceable and to give effect to the parties' intent. If a dispute arises as to (a) the CPI or a substitute index, (b) the Occupancy Rate, (c) the Breakpoint, or (d) the allocation of any Award, and the parties cannot resolve it within thirty (30) days, the matter shall be determined by an independent certified public accountant (as to clauses (a) through (c)) or a qualified appraiser (as to clause (d)), jointly selected by the parties, whose determination shall be final and binding and whose fees shall be borne equally.
@H2 18.4 Binding Effect; Successors
@P This Lease shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the parties and their respective successors, permitted assigns, heirs, and legal representatives. The rights of each Leasehold Mortgagee under Article 10 are intended to be enforceable by such Leasehold Mortgagee as a third-party beneficiary of this Lease.
@H2 18.5 No Partnership; No Broker
@P Nothing in this Lease creates a partnership, joint venture, or principal-agent relationship between the parties. Each party represents to the other that it has not dealt with any broker or finder in connection with this Lease, and each party shall indemnify the other against any brokerage claim arising from its own acts.
@H2 18.6 Survival
@P The provisions of this Lease that by their nature are intended to survive the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease, including Article 8, Article 10, Section 14.5, Section 16.5, Section 16.9, and this Article 18, shall so survive.
@H2 18.7 Counterparts; Electronic Signatures
@P This Lease may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original and all of which together shall constitute one instrument. Electronic signatures and electronically transmitted signatures shall be as effective as original signatures, provided that the parties shall, upon request, deliver original signature pages for recordation.
@H2 18.8 Time for Performance
@P Time is of the essence with respect to Landlord's obligations under this Lease. Time is not of the essence with respect to Tenant's obligations, except as expressly provided in Article 9 and in Section 16.1.
@H2 18.9 Exhibits
@P The following Exhibits are attached to and made a part of this Lease: **Exhibit A** (Legal Description of the Premises); **Exhibit B** (Permitted Exceptions); **Exhibit C** (Form of Letter of Credit); **Exhibit D** (Form of SNDA); **Exhibit E** (Project Program); **Exhibit F** (Form of Memorandum of Lease); **Exhibit G** (Form of Estoppel Certificate); and **Exhibit H** (Environmental Reports Index).
@H2 18.10 Interpretation of Conflicting Provisions
@P In the event of any conflict between the body of this Lease and any Exhibit, the body of this Lease shall control, except that the legal description in **Exhibit A** shall control as to the boundaries of the Premises and **Exhibit B** shall control as to the Permitted Exceptions. In the event of any conflict between this Lease and the Term Sheet, this Lease shall control.
@H2 18.11 Authority's Statutory Status
@P Nothing in this Lease shall be construed to require Landlord to take any action prohibited by its enabling legislation or by Applicable Law, or to pledge the full faith and credit of the City of Port Calloway. Landlord acknowledges, however, that the obligations it has undertaken in this Lease are valid and binding obligations payable from its general funds to the extent provided herein, and that it has obtained all approvals required to undertake them.
@H2 18.12 Counterpart Execution by the Leasehold Mortgagee
@P Each Leasehold Mortgagee may, at its election, execute this Lease for the sole purpose of acknowledging Article 10 and Section 17.4, without thereby becoming a party to this Lease or assuming any obligation of Tenant.

