@P This memorandum does three things. First, it identifies the twelve issues that we believe carry the greatest risk to closing, to financeability, or to the value of your leasehold. Second, it reconciles every figure, date, area, and cross-reference in the record against an independent computation, and records every conflict between documents. Third, it sets out an issue register of forty-seven items with a recommended drafting response for each, tied to the section of the draft Ground Lease in which the response appears.
@P Our overall assessment is that the Term Sheet is a workable business deal, but that it is not yet bankable, and that three provisions as drafted are unacceptable in their current form: the milestone reverter (Term Sheet Section 9), the fixed percentage-rent breakpoint (Section 6), and the tax abatement commencement date (Section 10). Two further items are prerequisites to closing that are not presently in hand: a corrected legal description, and a recorded amendment to the 2019 right of first refusal so that it does not reach a leasehold mortgagee's foreclosure. If those five items are not resolved, we do not believe Bayside Federal will close, and we do not believe the deal survives a lender's credit committee.

@H2 Top-Risk Register
